ats its ctrl arm by >= the 7.83 lift margin, strict-majority of seeds, EITHER rep; readiness = local_view_greedy + oracle clear the 1.0 floor @D3.", "notes": "MECH-457 GOV-FANOUT-1 H3 (credit-horizon) discrimination, routed by failure_autopsy_V3-EXQ-769_2026-07-17. DIAGNOSTIC (excluded from scoring); PROMOTES/DEMOTES NOTHING; route to /failure-autopsy (read jointly with H1 V3-EXQ-770 + H2 V3-EXQ-771). Manipulation = the TRAINING forage-credit DENSITY only (ctrl=sparse +1.0/contact, treat=dense potential-based shaping toward nearest resource, Ng et al. 1999 -- policy-invariant, telescopes to ~0 net return so it densifies credit without adding reward mass; EVAL unshaped for both). Capacity/drive/budget/env held at the NON-REGRESSED reference (128/3x/detached; NOT the 769-falsified 256/5x). RE-DERIVE BRAKE: PERMITS -- new EXQ NUMBER on a DIFFERENT design axis (measurement). NULL (dense credit still forages ~0 both reps) -> the wall is DEEPER than credit horizon (representation ceiling / different mechanism / approach-generation deficit). Anti-alias vs H1: H3 moves extrinsic forage-credit density; H1 moves the intrinsic-drive anneal schedule. Shaping is an experiment-layer PROBE (mech457_probe_envs.ForageShapingWrapper), NOT a ree_core feature (769 autopsy substrate action=none); an H3 WIN routes /implement-substrate. MECH-457 stays candidate/v3_pending.", "recording_schema": "rec/v1", "substrate_hash": "f56e1a7e1ce7721b9e4dd91b4da668f397ec005ce360cb0cdabd66610f2bbbde", "machine": "ree-cloud-4", "machine_class": "linux-x86_64-py3.10", "elapsed_seconds": 22830.663648, "seeds": [42, 43, 44], "queue_id": "V3-EXQ-772"}